            <ArticleTitle>Minimally invasive management of intrahepatic type II gallbladder perforation: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3978/j.issn.2304-3881.2015.08.02</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intrahepatic gallbladder perforation (GBP) is a rare medical entity, which creates a cholecystohepatic communication. We describe the case of a 70-year-old patient who presented with abdominal pain and a Niemeier type II GBP. This case report illustrates the minimally invasive management of a rare and life-threatening pathology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
